## 2. What Changed Since the Day 52 Version

- `src/components/` is confirmed still empty — correctly scheduled for Days 54-57, not built early.
- `scripts/build.js` is new: the Day 52 architecture called for "no build server," which today's implementation satisfies via a one-time local precompile script rather than a persistent dev server or webpack config.
- `public/index.html` is generated, not authored — added to `.gitignore` accordingly, with the GitHub Actions workflow updated to build it fresh on every deploy.
- `package.json` was not part of the Day 52 structure sketch; it's added today holding only build-time dependencies (no runtime framework dependency beyond the embedded UMD builds).

## 3. Folder Responsibilities (Unchanged Reasoning, Now With Real Files)

- **`src/data/`** — the synthetic data engine. All five files described in Day 52's plan are now real, working code, verified end-to-end via the Day 53 Hello World (see `DAY3-SUMMARY.md`).
- **`src/state/incidentState.js`** — the governance boundary. `submitSignOff` already enforces the sign-off gate today, even though no UI calls it yet. This was built now (Day 53) rather than Day 57 because it's foundational state management, not a feature — the Day 57 work is the *UI* for signing off, not the gate logic itself.
- **`src/components/`** stays empty on purpose — building it now would be exactly the "core feature work" this task explicitly says not to start yet.

## 4. Day 4 (Day 54) Readiness

Everything Day 54's Incident Queue UI needs already exists: `getIncidentQueue()` is implemented and tested (via the Hello World's debug summary), the design tokens are in place, and the bilingual shell renders. Day 54 can start directly on `IncidentQueue.jsx`, `IncidentCard.jsx`, and `SummaryStrip.jsx` with no further setup.
